                    new TheorySection { heading = "Confined areas", body = "A confined area is a landing site with obstacles close around it. Recce from height first: wind, size, slope, surface, obstacles and the way out. Approach into wind on a steeper path that clears the obstacles, and come to a hover before descending vertically. Plan the departure before you land: you need the power to climb vertically above the trees." },
                    new TheorySection { heading = "Slope landings", body = "Lower one skid onto the upslope side first, then lower the collective slowly while moving the cyclic into the slope to stop the aircraft sliding. Most light helicopters are limited to slopes of about 8 to 10 degrees; beyond that, find another spot." },
